00:43:35.990 --> 00:43:44.030
There's also a little thing that you can put on your finger that's like sort of meant to simulate an adult cat's tongue.
还有一个你可以套在手指上的小东西，有点像是为了模拟成年猫的舌头。

1179
00:43:44.030 --> 00:43:46.490
And if you foster kittens, you can get that.
如果你寄养小猫，你可以弄到那个。

1180
00:43:46.610 --> 00:43:48.690
And then you can like rub that between their eyes.
然后你就可以用那个在它们两眼之间擦一擦。

1181
00:43:48.870 --> 00:43:50.410
That's a thing you can get too.
这也是你可以买到的东西。

1182
00:43:51.290 --> 00:43:52.070
Cassie's in the booth.
凯西在录音间里。

1183
00:43:52.230 --> 00:43:54.370
Cassie, you just fostered a bunch of kittens.
凯西，你最近刚寄养了一窝小猫。

1184
00:43:54.510 --> 00:43:55.510
Did you lick any of them?
你舔过它们中的任何一只吗？

1185
00:43:56.190 --> 00:43:56.910
I didn't.
我没有。

1186
00:43:56.990 --> 00:44:00.110
I didn't know this was a thing, but maybe next round I'll try it.
我不知道还有这种操作，但也许下一轮我会试试。

1187
00:44:00.170 --> 00:44:02.250
Or you can just get the little finger brush thing.
或者你也可以直接买那个小手指刷。

1188
00:44:02.370 --> 00:44:05.090
That came out while I was like mid-fostering.
那玩意儿在我寄养进行到一半的时候推出了。

1189
00:44:05.090 --> 00:44:07.970
And I did move to the finger brush eventually.
我最后还是换成了手指刷。

1190
00:44:08.450 --> 00:44:08.830
Yeah.
对。

1191
00:44:08.890 --> 00:44:09.670
I'll get that.
我去买那个。

1192
00:44:09.750 --> 00:44:11.330
There was one that haunted me.
有一个东西让我挥之不去。

1193
00:44:11.450 --> 00:44:15.010
It's a thing that you can – well, I won't be able to unsee it.
那是一个你可以——好吧，我这辈子都忘不了这画面了。

1194
00:44:15.070 --> 00:44:19.030
It's a fake tongue that you can put in your mouth like a pacifier.
那是一个假舌头，你可以像安抚奶嘴一样把它含在嘴里。

1195
00:44:19.210 --> 00:44:19.570
Why?
为什么？

1196
00:44:19.750 --> 00:44:21.330
And then you can lick your cat.
然后你就可以舔你的猫了。

1197
00:44:21.430 --> 00:44:22.250
It can just be on your finger.
它也可以只是戴在你的手指上。

1198
00:44:22.370 --> 00:44:23.270
That's what she said.
这话听着可不对劲。

1199
00:44:25.290 --> 00:44:26.510
I'm showing Jenna.
我正在给珍娜看。

1200
00:44:26.870 --> 00:44:27.370
Oh, my God.
天哪。

1201
00:44:28.710 --> 00:44:30.010
Introducing Ricky Brush.
隆重介绍瑞奇·布拉什。

1202
00:44:31.270 --> 00:44:32.070
I'm sorry.
对不起。

1203
00:44:32.350 --> 00:44:32.830
Cassie.
卡茜。

1204
00:44:41.010 --> 00:44:47.710
It's also – it's also – they have like a – like a – like a – a big muscly
它还——它还——他们有一个像——像——像——一个肌肉发达的

1205
00:44:47.710 --> 00:44:49.850
man with a licky brush in his mouth.
男人，嘴里含着一把舔毛刷。

1206
00:44:49.850 --> 00:44:50.630
A pacifier.
一个安抚奶嘴。

1207
00:44:50.790 --> 00:44:55.330
It's a pacifier that has a tongue on it.
那是一个带有一截舌头的安抚奶嘴。

1208
00:44:55.350 --> 00:45:00.490
And he's – he's cradling his cat like a baby and then like licking it.
而且他——他像抱婴儿一样抱着他的猫，然后还在那儿舔它。

1209
00:45:00.490 --> 00:45:06.550
And it's just that they picked someone I would not expect.
关键是他们选了一个我怎么也想不到的人。

1210
00:45:06.730 --> 00:45:07.710
I mean –
我是说——

1211
00:45:07.710 --> 00:45:11.770
I want you to know I saw that and I have been waiting to show you.
我想让你知道我看到那个了，而且我一直等着拿给你看。

1212
00:45:11.890 --> 00:45:13.710
I was like, I'm not even going to tell her.
当时我想，我甚至不打算告诉她。

1213
00:45:13.810 --> 00:45:15.270
I want her to see it.
我要让她自己看。

1214
00:45:15.410 --> 00:45:17.430
I want to watch her react to it.
我想看她看到时的反应。

1215
00:45:17.530 --> 00:45:17.830
Oh, my God.
哦，天哪。

1216
00:45:17.830 --> 00:45:20.030
Because I was like, what is happening?
因为当时我想，这到底是怎么回事？

1217
00:45:20.210 --> 00:45:21.450
What did I just click on?
我刚才点了个什么东西？

1218
00:45:23.890 --> 00:45:24.330
Wow.
哇。

1219
00:45:24.330 --> 00:45:24.710
Okay.
好吧。

1220
00:45:24.710 --> 00:45:29.630
Well, I guess it can take the idea of bonding with your cat to a whole new level.
好吧，我想这把与猫咪建立亲密感这事带到了一个全新的高度。

1221
00:45:29.950 --> 00:45:33.230
They make them for your fingers, is what I want to say.
我是想说，他们甚至还为你的手指做了一个。

1222
00:45:33.770 --> 00:45:39.370
To finish out this cat storyline, Angela returns to the office.
为了收尾这个关于猫的剧情线，安吉拉回到了办公室。

1223
00:45:39.550 --> 00:45:39.930
Yes.
对。

1224
00:45:40.190 --> 00:45:43.970
And she sees her computer is on and she's like, oh, my gosh.
然后她看到自己的电脑开着，她就想，哦，天哪。

1225
00:45:44.270 --> 00:45:45.990
Has that been on the whole time?
这电脑一直开着吗？

1226
00:45:46.570 --> 00:45:49.490
And Kevin and Oscar are like, what?
然后凯文和奥斯卡就说，什么？

1227
00:45:49.630 --> 00:45:52.570
I don't – we were just – we don't have no idea what you're talking about.
我才不——我们只是——我们根本不知道你在说什么。

1228
00:45:52.570 --> 00:45:58.910
Oscar has a talking head where he says he needs to erase that image from his head.
奥斯卡有一个单采访镜头，他说他需要把那个画面从脑子里删掉。

1229
00:45:59.810 --> 00:46:03.850
But then Angela coughs up a hairball.
但接着安吉拉咳出一个毛球。

1230
00:46:04.970 --> 00:46:06.110
Well, I –
这个嘛，我——

1231
00:46:06.110 --> 00:46:07.070
Let's hear about that.
我们来听听这个。

1232
00:46:07.190 --> 00:46:09.550
I cough up a tiny hair, guys, right?
我咳出了一根细小的头发，伙计们，对吧？

1233
00:46:09.550 --> 00:46:10.930
It's like a little hair.
就像一根小头发。

1234
00:46:11.610 --> 00:46:12.730
But you know what?
但你知道吗？

1235
00:46:12.830 --> 00:46:15.630
You've had your cat, like, cough up a hairball, right?
你们都见过自己的猫咳出毛球，对吧？

1236
00:46:15.650 --> 00:46:16.790
It's so violent.
那场面太惨烈了。

1237
00:46:17.010 --> 00:46:17.770
It's like –
就像——

1238
00:46:17.770 --> 00:46:18.270
Yeah.
是啊。

1239
00:46:18.850 --> 00:46:20.410
Oh, oh, oh, oh, oh.
哦，哦，哦，哦，哦。

1240
00:46:21.050 --> 00:46:23.770
It's so incredibly –
这简直是——

1241
00:46:23.770 --> 00:46:23.970
I know.
我知道。

1242
00:46:24.150 --> 00:46:26.670
The first time you get a cat and they do it, you're like, oh, my God.
你第一次养猫，当它们这么做时，你会想，哦，天哪。

1243
00:46:26.990 --> 00:46:28.070
I don't know what's happening.
我不知道发生什么事了。

1244
00:46:30.010 --> 00:46:31.030
It's so intense.
太激烈了。

1245
00:46:32.070 --> 00:46:36.190
So, once again, Ken and I and Mindy were talking about how big do you go here, right?
所以，再次说明，肯、我和敏迪当时在讨论这里尺度该有多大，对吧？

1246
00:46:36.510 --> 00:46:39.110
How big do I really – because you have two choices.
我究竟该把尺度放大到什么程度——因为你有两种选择。

1247
00:46:39.670 --> 00:46:42.110
Either Angela Martin has to do that, like –
要么安吉拉·马丁必须做出那种——

1248
00:46:43.630 --> 00:46:45.370
Or it's, like, way more subtle.
要么就是，那种低调得多。

1249
00:46:45.710 --> 00:46:51.950
And so, I practiced a few different ways, and this is the one they liked, where basically I'm just pulling one hair off my tongue.
所以，我练习了几种不同的方式，这是他们最喜欢的一种，基本上我只是从舌头上扯下一根头发。

1250
00:46:52.310 --> 00:46:54.350
And it's like – what is it?
然后就像是——这到底是什么？

1251
00:46:54.410 --> 00:46:55.350
Was it the cat?
是那只猫吗？

1252
00:46:55.610 --> 00:46:56.810
Is it something else?
还是别的原因？

1253
00:46:56.990 --> 00:46:57.750
It was the cat.
就是那只猫。

1254
00:46:57.750 --> 00:46:58.350
It was the cat.
就是那只猫。

1255
00:46:58.450 --> 00:46:59.130
It was the cat.
就是那只猫。

1256
00:46:59.130 --> 00:46:59.730
It was.
就是。

1257
00:46:59.750 --> 00:47:04.430
But I had to do it enough to sell it to Oscar and not so much that it was, like, a total cartoon.
但我要做到足以向奥斯卡交差，又不能太夸张，免得看起来像个纯粹的动画片。

1258
00:47:04.790 --> 00:47:06.150
That was my work day, guys.
这就是我的工作日，各位。

1259
00:47:12.170 --> 00:47:14.830
Lick a cat, and then cough up a hairball.
舔一只猫，然后咳出一团毛球。

1260
00:47:15.170 --> 00:47:16.350
Mom, what did you do at work today?
妈妈，你今天在工作时做什么了？

1261
00:47:16.910 --> 00:47:18.070
Welcome to Hollywood.
欢迎来到好莱坞。

1262
00:47:18.650 --> 00:47:20.570
Should we go to Nashua?
我们该去纳舒厄吗？

1263
00:47:20.890 --> 00:47:24.970
We do, because Pam has talked Michael into giving his presentation.
我们得去，因为帕姆说服了迈克尔做他的演讲。

1264
00:47:25.210 --> 00:47:30.610
Because then maybe they'll all talk about how great Michael was, and Holly will hear about it, right?
因为那样也许他们都会讨论迈克尔有多棒，霍莉也会听到，对吧？

1265
00:47:30.770 --> 00:47:33.410
That's the way you show AJ, right?
这就是你向AJ证明自己的方式，对吧？

1266
00:47:33.890 --> 00:47:34.410
Yes.
是的。

1267
00:47:34.810 --> 00:47:35.510
And you know what?
而且你知道吗？

1268
00:47:35.630 --> 00:47:37.630
At the beginning, it's going great.
一开始，一切都进行得很顺利。

1269
00:47:38.250 --> 00:47:38.950
It is.
确实很顺利。

1270
00:47:39.110 --> 00:47:40.610
He's doing a fantastic job.
他干得棒极了。

1271
00:47:40.610 --> 00:47:42.790
Just listen to all of his movie references.
听听他用的那些电影梗就知道了。

1272
00:47:44.670 --> 00:47:48.290
Good morning, Vietnashua!
早上好，越战纳舒厄！

1273
00:47:51.100 --> 00:47:51.900
Sales.
销售。

1274
00:47:52.300 --> 00:47:56.400
Sales is what brings us together today.
销售才是今天将我们聚在一起的纽带。

1275
00:47:57.720 --> 00:48:02.500
How do we deal with clients who say,
我们该如何应对那些说出这种话的客户——

1276
00:48:03.220 --> 00:48:06.720
Frankly, my dear, I don't give a damn about paper,
说实话，亲爱的，我才不在乎什么纸张呢，

1277
00:48:06.840 --> 00:48:09.900
and get them to show us the money?
并让他们把钱掏出来？

1278
00:48:10.820 --> 00:48:13.260
Well, we are going to find out today.
好吧，我们今天就要找出答案。

1279
00:48:14.060 --> 00:48:15.540
I had written this down.
我之前把这个记下来了。

1280
00:48:15.980 --> 00:48:17.980
It's so interesting that you played that clip,
你放这段视频真的很有意思，

1281
00:48:18.000 --> 00:48:20.040
because I wondered,
因为我在想，

1282
00:48:20.420 --> 00:48:25.080
do our younger viewers get all of the references in Michael's opening remarks?
我们的年轻观众能听懂迈克尔开场白里的所有梗吗？

1283
00:48:25.240 --> 00:48:26.620
Do they know these movies?
他们知道这些电影吗？

1284
00:48:26.920 --> 00:48:27.760
Good Morning Vietnam,
《早安越南》，

1285
00:48:28.180 --> 00:48:29.380
Princess Bride,
《公主新娘》，

1286
00:48:29.740 --> 00:48:30.700
Gone with the Wind,
《乱世佳人》，

1287
00:48:30.860 --> 00:48:31.840
and Jerry Maguire.
以及《甜心先生》。

1288
00:48:31.840 --> 00:48:34.840
I guess this is Michael's taste in movies.
我猜这就是迈克尔的电影品味。

1289
00:48:35.040 --> 00:48:35.320
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1290
00:48:35.740 --> 00:48:37.440
But do people know all those today?
但现在的人都了解这些吗？

1291
00:48:37.800 --> 00:48:40.860
I mean, you've got to know Princess Bride, right?
我的意思是，总得知道《公主新娘》吧？

1292
00:48:41.100 --> 00:48:41.800
I think.
我想是的。

1293
00:48:42.580 --> 00:48:43.720
I don't know.
我不知道。

1294
00:48:44.160 --> 00:48:45.440
I don't know.
我不知道。

1295
00:48:45.940 --> 00:48:47.260
But he's got them.
但他把他们拿下了。

1296
00:48:47.360 --> 00:48:48.020
They're laughing.
他们在笑。

1297
00:48:48.100 --> 00:48:51.220
They love his, like, voices he's doing.
他们很喜欢他模仿的那些声音。

1298
00:48:51.660 --> 00:48:53.200
Nashua likes Michael.
纳舒厄很喜欢迈克尔。

1299
00:48:53.200 --> 00:48:56.320
From the receptionist to his opening remarks,
从前台接待到他的开场白，

1300
00:48:56.320 --> 00:48:58.180
they're eating out of the palm of his hand.
他们都被他迷得团团转。

1301
00:48:58.280 --> 00:49:00.720
If only he could get over this Holly thing,
要是他能放下霍莉这件事，

1302
00:49:00.720 --> 00:49:05.560
he would finally have a day where he was the king of comedy like he's always wanted.
他终于能迎来属于自己的一天，像他一直渴望的那样成为喜剧之王。

1303
00:49:05.760 --> 00:49:09.720
Those 30 seconds you just heard are the best that it is,
刚才你听到的那30秒已经是绝佳的状态了，

1304
00:49:09.840 --> 00:49:11.680
because that's how quickly it falls apart.
因为情况崩盘就是这么快。

1305
00:49:12.020 --> 00:49:15.200
Because Michael zeroes in on AJ.
因为迈克尔把矛头对准了AJ。

1306
00:49:15.480 --> 00:49:16.360
He can't help it.
他忍不住。

1307
00:49:17.200 --> 00:49:17.680
Salesmen.
销售员。

1308
00:49:18.940 --> 00:49:19.420
Salespeople.
销售人员。

1309
00:49:20.100 --> 00:49:22.380
He's going to pick a random salesperson.
他要随便挑一个销售人员。

1310
00:49:22.500 --> 00:49:23.180
You there, sir.
就是你，先生。

1311
00:49:23.360 --> 00:49:23.640
You.
你。

1312
00:49:23.960 --> 00:49:24.380
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1313
00:49:25.000 --> 00:49:26.480
What's it like to be you?
做你自己是什么感觉？

1314
00:49:26.680 --> 00:49:28.080
Oh, here we go.
哦，开始了。

1315
00:49:28.240 --> 00:49:28.420
Yeah.
是啊。

1316
00:49:28.680 --> 00:49:31.700
And then Michael has a full-on panic attack.
然后迈克尔就彻底恐慌发作了。

1317
00:49:31.900 --> 00:49:35.160
He winds up on the ground, and he crawls out of the room.
他倒在地上，然后从房间里爬了出去。

1318
00:49:35.260 --> 00:49:35.540
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1319
00:49:35.980 --> 00:49:37.120
Leaving Pam.
留下了帕姆。

1320
00:49:37.900 --> 00:49:38.380
Yeah.
是啊。

1321
00:49:39.160 --> 00:49:42.160
Well, before we get to what Pam is going to do,
好吧，在我们聊帕姆要做什么之前，

1322
00:49:42.280 --> 00:49:44.900
I wanted to shout out a few crew cameos.
我想鸣谢几个客串出镜的工作人员。

1323
00:49:45.440 --> 00:49:46.120
Oh, okay.
哦，好的。

1324
00:49:46.660 --> 00:49:48.580
So, sitting next to AJ,
所以，坐在AJ旁边，

1325
00:49:48.980 --> 00:49:52.780
the woman who asked the question about discounts from distributors,
那个问关于经销商折扣问题的女士，

1326
00:49:52.780 --> 00:49:54.620
that was Mary Wall.
那是玛丽·沃尔。

1327
00:49:54.940 --> 00:49:55.500
Yes.
对。

1328
00:49:55.680 --> 00:49:57.640
And she was a member of our production staff,
她曾是我们制作团队的一员，

1329
00:49:57.640 --> 00:50:00.880
and she is delightful and wonderful.
她非常可爱又棒极了。

1330
00:50:01.360 --> 00:50:04.600
She has gone on to become a producer and a director.
她后来成了一名制片人和导演。

1331
00:50:04.920 --> 00:50:08.460
She currently is working on a documentary called The Fan Connection.
她目前正在制作一部名为《球迷情缘》的纪录片。

1332
00:50:08.620 --> 00:50:12.480
You can actually check it out at fanconnectionmovie.com.
你其实可以在fanconnectionmovie.com上了解一下。

1333
00:50:12.540 --> 00:50:13.320
You can see a trailer.
你可以看到预告片。

1334
00:50:13.320 --> 00:50:16.580
It's all about the hockey fans in Buffalo.
讲的全是布法罗的冰球迷。

1335
00:50:17.040 --> 00:50:18.160
Oh, I would love that.
哦，我肯定会喜欢这个。

1336
00:50:18.160 --> 00:50:19.940
And their commitment to their hockey team.
以及他们对冰球队的执着。

1337
00:50:20.020 --> 00:50:21.100
And you know I love hockey.
而且你知道我喜欢冰球。

1338
00:50:21.320 --> 00:50:23.240
So, anyway, check out the trailer, guys.
总之，大家去看看预告片吧。

1339
00:50:23.480 --> 00:50:24.820
I love sports documentaries.
我喜欢体育纪录片。

1340
00:50:25.200 --> 00:50:25.540
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1341
00:50:25.540 --> 00:50:26.080
Love them.
超爱。

1342
00:50:26.260 --> 00:50:31.660
And then, sitting in the row in front of AJ with the red hair,
然后，坐在AJ前面一排、留着红发的，

1343
00:50:31.900 --> 00:50:34.640
was Claire Scanlon, our editor.
是我们的剪辑师克莱尔·斯坎伦。

1344
00:50:34.980 --> 00:50:36.880
And Pam's going to call her Freckles.
帕姆要叫她小雀斑。

1345
00:50:37.200 --> 00:50:41.780
Claire is a full-on badass, amazing editor, and now prolific director.
克莱尔是个彻头彻尾的狠角色、了不起的剪辑师，现在也是个高产的导演。

1346
00:50:41.780 --> 00:50:42.300
Yes.
对。

1347
00:50:42.520 --> 00:50:46.620
And then I have another guest star I want to mention, Michael McCartney.
然后我还要提另一位客串明星，迈克尔·麦卡特尼。

1348
00:50:46.880 --> 00:50:49.440
He played the other Nashua employee who says,
他饰演了另一个纳舒厄员工，也就是那个说，

1349
00:50:49.580 --> 00:50:51.440
what does this have to do with sales?
这和销售有什么关系？

1350
00:50:52.080 --> 00:50:54.460
When Michael is disintegrating.
当迈克尔情绪崩溃的时候。

1351
00:50:54.920 --> 00:50:56.960
He has a very extensive resume.
他的简历非常丰富。

1352
00:50:57.420 --> 00:51:01.440
He is the producer and director of the series The Millionaires on Amazon Prime.
他是亚马逊 Prime 平台剧集《百万富翁》的制片人和导演。

1353
00:51:01.440 --> 00:51:03.120
But here's what I want to tell you.
但接下来我要告诉你的是。

1354
00:51:03.340 --> 00:51:03.540
What?
什么？

1355
00:51:03.540 --> 00:51:05.300
This is the first time I've seen this.
这是我第一次看到这个。

1356
00:51:05.480 --> 00:51:08.600
And all of my Googling of all of our guest stars,
我用谷歌搜索了我们所有的客串明星，

1357
00:51:09.020 --> 00:51:10.820
well, now I don't know what to expect.
好吧，现在我不知道该期待什么了。

1358
00:51:11.780 --> 00:51:15.460
Michael McCartney has been on Law & Order.
迈克尔·麦卡特尼演过《法律与秩序》。

1359
00:51:15.760 --> 00:51:16.100
Okay.
好的。

1360
00:51:16.380 --> 00:51:17.780
Law & Order SVU.
《法律与秩序：特殊受害者》。

1361
00:51:17.940 --> 00:51:18.460
Oh, well.
噢，好吧。

1362
00:51:19.040 --> 00:51:21.780
And Law & Order Criminal Intent.
还有《法律与秩序：犯罪倾向》。

1363
00:51:21.980 --> 00:51:23.220
The trifecta.
大满贯。

1364
00:51:23.540 --> 00:51:24.440
Holy cow!
我的天哪！

1365
00:51:24.820 --> 00:51:25.300
All three.
全演过了。

1366
00:51:26.000 --> 00:51:26.920
Not on Monk.
没演过《神探阿蒙》。

1367
00:51:27.280 --> 00:51:28.180
Not on Monk.
没演过《神探阿蒙》。

1368
00:51:28.580 --> 00:51:29.660
There's still room.
还有空间。

1369
00:51:29.840 --> 00:51:30.440
There's still room.
还有空间。

1370
00:51:30.540 --> 00:51:33.840
Future guest star, if you could be on all three Law & Orders and Monk,
未来的客串明星，如果你能把三部《法律与秩序》和《神探阿蒙》全演一遍，

1371
00:51:33.960 --> 00:51:35.940
I'm going to drive to your house and give you a cake.
我要开车去你家送你一块蛋糕。

1372
00:51:37.680 --> 00:51:42.480
So, when I was trading emails with Rob, I was like, Rob, you've got to share what it was like in that room
所以，当我跟罗布发邮件时，我说，罗布，你得跟大家分享一下在那间会议室里的感受，

1373
00:51:43.100 --> 00:51:45.880
when Steve, as Michael, is falling apart.
当时史蒂夫饰演的迈克尔情绪崩溃。

1374
00:51:46.180 --> 00:51:46.540
Yes.
是的。

1375
00:51:46.940 --> 00:51:48.260
And singling you out.
而且还针对你。

1376
00:51:48.780 --> 00:51:49.820
I mean, I don't know.
我是说，我不知道。

1377
00:51:49.900 --> 00:51:50.620
How did you do that?
你是怎么做到的？

1378
00:51:50.680 --> 00:51:51.600
How did you get through it?
你是怎么挺过去的？

1379
00:51:51.600 --> 00:51:52.720
And here's what he had to say.
以下是他的回应。

1380
00:51:53.180 --> 00:52:02.260
My memories of shooting that scene in the conference room with Steve are mostly about just trying not to laugh
我拍摄那场在会议室和史蒂夫对戏的场景的记忆，大多都是关于努力克制自己别笑场，

1381
00:52:02.260 --> 00:52:13.720
because sometimes I just start laughing when people are funny because, really, I feel like a lot of times on comedy shows,
因为有时候别人搞笑时我就会忍不住笑起来，真的，我觉得很多时候在喜剧节目里，

1382
00:52:14.420 --> 00:52:17.580
you're trying to make the other person laugh.
你都在试图逗笑对方。

1383
00:52:17.580 --> 00:52:21.380
In a way, you're kind of trying to f*** with them a little bit.
某种程度上，你其实有点想整整他们。

1384
00:52:21.620 --> 00:52:28.840
So, anyway, I was just trying to keep a straight face because Steve is so funny and Jenna is so funny
所以，总之，我只是在努力保持面不改色，因为史蒂夫太搞笑了，珍娜也太搞笑了，

1385
00:52:28.840 --> 00:52:30.540
and everybody on the show is so funny.
剧里的每个人都太搞笑了。

1386
00:52:30.620 --> 00:52:31.920
And I also get very nervous.
而且我也很容易紧张。

1387
00:52:31.920 --> 00:52:39.700
I get nervous going into a new show and, you know, there's this whole other culture there already established.
我进一个新的剧组会感到紧张，而且，你知道的，那里已经有一种完全成熟的文化了。

1388
00:52:39.700 --> 00:52:44.940
When you're a guest actor on a show, it's different because you don't know what you're walking into.
当你是剧中的客串演员时，情况有所不同，因为你不知道自己将要面对的是什么。

1389
00:52:45.300 --> 00:52:49.620
So, I was a little bit nervous and Steve is just, you know, iconic.
所以，我当时有点紧张，而且史蒂夫，你知道的，简直是标志性人物。

1390
00:52:49.900 --> 00:52:51.060
Steve is just so funny.
史蒂夫实在是太搞笑了。

1391
00:52:51.300 --> 00:53:01.740
And when he's kind of coming at me like that, he's, you know, putting me down and ignoring me and calling me names in a very funny way.
当他那样冲着我来的时候，你知道，他贬低我、忽视我，用一种非常搞笑的方式叫我绰号。

1392
00:53:01.920 --> 00:53:04.740
But it's all so funny.
但这一切都太搞笑了。

1393
00:53:04.820 --> 00:53:06.960
So, mostly trying not to laugh.
所以，主要就是在努力憋笑。

1394
00:53:07.980 --> 00:53:12.440
I loved his description of what it's like to be a guest actor on a show.
我很喜欢他对作为一名客串演员身处剧组中的感受的描述。

1395
00:53:13.020 --> 00:53:20.000
Walking into the world and it's a comedy and it's supposed to be funny, but then you're not supposed to laugh.
走进这个世界，这是一部喜剧，本来就该搞笑，但你又偏偏不能笑。

1396
00:53:20.000 --> 00:53:22.800
I just, I related to all of that so much.
我真的是对这一切感同身受。

1397
00:53:22.960 --> 00:53:23.520
I did too.
我也是。

1398
00:53:23.520 --> 00:53:29.040
Well, we also asked him, does he still get recognized as AJ?
对了，我们还问了他，现在走在路上还会被认出是 AJ 吗？

1399
00:53:29.460 --> 00:53:32.520
He's been on, what did you say, 140?
他演过，你刚才说多少部？

1400
00:53:33.120 --> 00:53:35.560
140 movies and TV shows.
140 部电影和电视剧。

1401
00:53:35.880 --> 00:53:37.600
Does he get recognized as AJ?
他会被认出是 AJ 吗？

1402
00:53:37.900 --> 00:53:38.880
Let's find out.
我们来看看。

1403
00:53:39.580 --> 00:53:43.480
Do I get recognized as AJ from The Office?
我会被认出是《办公室》里的 AJ 吗？

1404
00:53:43.480 --> 00:53:45.280
Are you kidding me?
你在开玩笑吧？

1405
00:53:45.280 --> 00:53:46.020
Yes.
是的。

1406
00:53:47.500 --> 00:53:48.580
Yes, a lot.
是的，经常。

1407
00:53:48.740 --> 00:53:50.880
And I'm so thankful for it.
我对此非常感激。

1408
00:53:50.940 --> 00:53:53.980
It is very fun to be recognized.
被人认出来是一件很有趣的事。

1409
00:53:54.060 --> 00:53:59.380
No matter what people tell you, it is fun because it's, you know, it's people love it.
不管别人怎么对你说，这真的很有趣，因为你知道，大家都很喜欢。

1410
00:53:59.500 --> 00:54:03.000
They love the show and that's fun.
他们喜欢这部剧，这就很有趣。

1411
00:54:03.260 --> 00:54:09.320
You know, like everyone had an opinion about Michael and Holly's relationship and I was just standing in the way.
你知道的，就像每个人对迈克尔和霍莉的关系都有看法，而我恰好挡在中间。

1412
00:54:09.480 --> 00:54:11.240
So, I would get threatened by strangers.
所以，我经常受到陌生人的威胁。

1413
00:54:11.240 --> 00:54:13.320
You know, it was crazy.
你知道，这太疯狂了。

1414
00:54:13.560 --> 00:54:16.580
In fact, people used to come up to me out of the blue.
事实上，人们以前经常无缘无故地走过来找我。

1415
00:54:16.820 --> 00:54:24.060
I remember people would sometimes whisper in my ear, like come up behind me and say, you stay away from Holly.
我记得有人有时会在我耳边低语，比如从我身后走过来对我说，离霍莉远点。

1416
00:54:24.280 --> 00:54:25.740
You stay away from Holly.
离霍莉远点。

1417
00:54:26.240 --> 00:54:30.600
And what's crazy is that my wife in real life, her name is Holly.
而疯狂的是，我现实生活中的妻子，她的名字就叫霍莉。

1418
00:54:30.600 --> 00:54:41.480
So, I would have to decide in about two seconds, okay, is this someone that used to date my wife in real life that I should murder?
所以，我必须在大约两秒钟内做出决定，好吧，这究竟是我妻子现实生活中以前的约会对象，我该把他干掉？

1419
00:54:41.980 --> 00:54:46.720
Or is this just a fan of The Office acting like a creeper?
还是这只是一个行为诡异的《办公室》粉丝？

1420
00:54:47.580 --> 00:54:50.140
I love that his wife's name is Holly.
我太喜欢他妻子叫霍莉这事了。

1421
00:54:50.380 --> 00:54:51.020
I know!
我懂！

1422
00:54:51.220 --> 00:54:52.020
That's insane.
这太疯狂了。

1423
00:54:52.260 --> 00:54:56.140
That is crazy though that people go up to him and they're like, leave Holly alone.
不过人们居然走过去对他说，离霍莉远点，这也太疯狂了。

1424
00:54:56.340 --> 00:54:57.160
And he's like, wait, what?
而他的反应是，等等，什么？

1425
00:54:57.160 --> 00:54:58.200
Wait, wait, that's my wife.
等等，等等，那是我妻子。

1426
00:54:58.280 --> 00:54:59.940
Oh, you're, oh, okay.
哦，你是，哦，好吧。

1427
00:55:00.100 --> 00:55:01.060
Oh, I know what you are.
哦，我知道你是什么人了。

1428
00:55:01.400 --> 00:55:01.760
Amazing.
太棒了。

1429
00:55:02.220 --> 00:55:04.840
Well, thank you, Rob, for sending in your audio clips.
那么，罗布，谢谢你发来你的音频剪辑。

1430
00:55:04.980 --> 00:55:06.080
It was so nice of you.
你真是太好了。

1431
00:55:06.240 --> 00:55:07.800
I love listening to your voice.
我喜欢听你的声音。

1432
00:55:08.040 --> 00:55:10.000
I think he has a soothing, pleasant voice.
我觉得他的声音听起来很舒缓、很悦耳。

1433
00:55:10.340 --> 00:55:11.780
Rob, she's not kidding.
罗布，她可不是在开玩笑。

1434
00:55:11.980 --> 00:55:18.300
While we were recording this episode and you sent in your audio clips, Jenna was like, I just love the sound of his voice.
在我们录制这一集、你发来音频剪辑的时候，珍娜就说，我太喜欢他说话的声音了。

1435
00:55:18.300 --> 00:55:18.860
I know.
我懂。

1436
00:55:18.860 --> 00:55:23.000
I hope you get tons of voiceover work because I would buy anything you're selling.
我希望你能接到大量配音工作，因为你卖什么我都会买。

1437
00:55:23.600 --> 00:55:24.020
Hey!
嘿！

1438
00:55:24.360 --> 00:55:24.600
Yeah.
对。

1439
00:55:24.800 --> 00:55:25.840
How about them apples?
你觉得这怎么样？

1440
00:55:26.600 --> 00:55:29.000
So, Jenna, Michael has left.
那么，珍娜，迈克尔已经走了。

1441
00:55:29.520 --> 00:55:30.460
Pam is in charge.
帕姆负责了。

1442
00:55:30.860 --> 00:55:34.000
She goes right into Forrest Gump.
她直接用起了《阿甘正传》的梗。

1443
00:55:34.640 --> 00:55:39.800
Lady, this was one of my favorite shooting days ever, having to take over the presentation.
姑娘，这是我拍戏有史以来最喜欢的日子之一，得接管那个演示环节。

1444
00:55:40.100 --> 00:55:41.880
It was so fun to watch you.
看你表演太有意思了。

1445
00:55:42.020 --> 00:55:42.900
It was hilarious.
太搞笑了。

1446
00:55:43.280 --> 00:55:47.340
I loved watching Pam try to do Michael's movie bits.
我特别喜欢看帕姆模仿迈克尔的电影桥段。

1447
00:55:47.780 --> 00:55:49.700
Angela, you know I'm not great with accents.
安吉拉，你知道我不太擅长模仿口音。

1448
00:55:49.960 --> 00:55:50.920
I know this.
我知道这点。

1449
00:55:51.020 --> 00:55:51.720
Or impressions.
或是模仿别人。

1450
00:55:51.720 --> 00:55:57.420
I cannot tell you how hard I worked on that Forrest Gump voice.
我简直无法形容我为了练那个《阿甘正传》的嗓音费了多大劲。

1451
00:55:57.920 --> 00:55:59.200
Oh, my gosh, lady.
噢，天哪，大姐。

1452
00:55:59.460 --> 00:56:00.260
So hard.
太难了。

1453
00:56:00.500 --> 00:56:03.580
Lady, I thought you were doing a bit to be bad, right?
大姐，我还以为你是在故意装演得不好，对吧？

1454
00:56:04.040 --> 00:56:04.600
Yes.
是的。

1455
00:56:04.600 --> 00:56:08.500
And that is what Mindy and Ken Kwapis thought on set.
而这正是明迪和肯·クワピス在片场时的想法。

1456
00:56:08.960 --> 00:56:11.680
They were crying laughing when I did it.
我演的时候他们都笑哭了。

1457
00:56:12.040 --> 00:56:16.040
Mindy said it was genius that I was doing it so bad.
明迪说我演得这么烂简直是天才。

1458
00:56:16.160 --> 00:56:16.500
Yeah.
对。

1459
00:56:16.740 --> 00:56:21.740
And I was texting with her because I was like, Mindy, do you remember this episode?
我还给她发短信，因为我就在想，明迪，你还记得这一集吗？

1460
00:56:21.740 --> 00:56:25.240
And she said, yes, I thought you were so funny that day.
她说，记得，我觉得那天你太搞笑了。

1461
00:56:25.420 --> 00:56:26.640
You're Forrest Gump.
你就是阿甘。

1462
00:56:26.820 --> 00:56:30.240
It was such a funny choice, you know, to be bad.
选择演得这么烂，真的是个超级搞笑的选择，你知道吧。

1463
00:56:30.780 --> 00:56:34.400
And I was like, Mindy, that was my literal best effort.
然后我说，明迪，那可是我字面意义上全力以赴的水平啊。

1464
00:56:35.640 --> 00:56:39.300
My acting limitations made me genius.
我演技的局限性让我成了天才。

1465
00:56:39.520 --> 00:56:47.420
Like, that's one of those things where, like, if I tried to be bad, it wouldn't have been as good as me giving it my best effort.
就像那种情况，如果我是故意想演砸，反而还不如我拼尽全力演得好呢。

1466
00:56:47.640 --> 00:56:49.160
I can't do it better than that.
我根本不可能比那演得更好了。

1467
00:56:49.260 --> 00:56:50.100
I need to hear it.
我得听听。

1468
00:56:50.200 --> 00:56:51.080
I need to hear it.
我得听听。

1469
00:56:51.080 --> 00:56:52.000
I got to hear it.
我必须得听听。

1470
00:56:52.080 --> 00:56:52.940
I got to hear it.
我得听听。

1471
00:56:53.040 --> 00:56:53.880
I'm getting my laptop.
我去拿我的笔记本电脑。

1472
00:56:53.980 --> 00:56:54.740
I got to hear it.
我得听听。

1473
00:56:55.040 --> 00:57:03.280
I got, now, with that information in my brain, I've got to hear it because I thought, like Mindy, that you were doing a bit.
我现在知道了这个信息，我非听不可了，因为我和明迪一样，以为你是在搞笑整蛊。

1474
00:57:03.720 --> 00:57:04.160
No.
没有。

1475
00:57:04.500 --> 00:57:05.800
At, like, I'm going to read it.
就好像，我要读一下。

1476
00:57:06.140 --> 00:57:08.040
My first gump, kind of crappy.
我的阿甘，有点烂。

1477
00:57:08.420 --> 00:57:10.440
But no, it was your best effort, honey.
但不是，亲爱的，那已经是你全力以赴了。

1478
00:57:10.600 --> 00:57:17.140
I listened to his voice in my head over and over and over and over again, and I tried to mimic it perfectly.
我脑子里一遍又一遍、一遍又一遍地听着他的声音，我试图完美地模仿它。

1479
00:57:17.140 --> 00:57:23.640
I have never loved you more, knowing now that that Forrest Gump was your earnest best effort.
现在知道那个阿甘是你认认真真拼尽全力演出来的，我简直不能更爱你了。

1480
00:57:23.780 --> 00:57:24.220
It was.
确实是。

1481
00:57:25.780 --> 00:57:28.620
Sales is like a box of chocolates.
销售就像一盒巧克力。

1482
00:57:28.920 --> 00:57:32.140
You never know which vendor you're going to get.
你永远不知道会遇到哪个供应商。

1483
00:57:34.300 --> 00:57:35.200
Forrest Gump.
阿甘。

1484
00:57:35.980 --> 00:57:36.660
Lady.
大姐。

1485
00:57:36.660 --> 00:57:39.340
That's the cutest thing ever.
这简直是史上最可爱的事了。

1486
00:57:39.640 --> 00:57:41.440
That is the cutest thing.
这太可爱了。

1487
00:57:41.700 --> 00:57:42.260
Oh, my gosh.
噢，天哪。

1488
00:57:42.420 --> 00:57:44.020
Look at Devin and Cassie.
看德文和卡西。

1489
00:57:44.160 --> 00:57:46.040
They're cracking up.
他们笑疯了。

1490
00:57:46.360 --> 00:57:48.220
You guys, is that adorable?
大家伙儿，这难道不萌吗？

1491
00:57:48.700 --> 00:57:49.360
Come on.
拜托。

1492
00:57:49.920 --> 00:57:50.640
So cute.
太可爱了。

1493
00:57:50.800 --> 00:57:51.420
We love it.
我们太喜欢了。

1494
00:57:52.140 --> 00:57:52.880
Thank you, guys.
谢谢大家。

1495
00:57:53.240 --> 00:57:53.920
Thank you.
谢谢。

1496
00:57:53.920 --> 00:57:56.040
I love doing that scene.
我好喜欢拍那一场戏。

1497
00:57:56.260 --> 00:57:57.800
I loved the chainsaw.
我好喜欢那把电锯。

1498
00:57:58.080 --> 00:57:59.140
I loved the chainsaw.
我好喜欢那把电锯。

1499
00:57:59.140 --> 00:58:07.760
It was one of my most, you know, this was one of the few times when I was called upon to do, like, what would you call it?
那是我经历过为数不多的几次，怎么说呢，被要求去做的那种，你管这叫什么来着？

1500
00:58:07.940 --> 00:58:09.160
Like, lead the group?
比如，领导大家？

1501
00:58:09.360 --> 00:58:11.060
To be the comedy protagoniSt.
成为喜剧的主角。

1502
00:58:11.480 --> 00:58:11.660
Yes.
是的。

1503
00:58:11.660 --> 00:58:13.820
I was usually the receiver of comedy.
我通常是喜剧效果的承受者。

1504
00:58:13.980 --> 00:58:19.480
My job on this show was to amplify a comedic moment with my deadpan reaction.
我在这个节目里的工作，就是用我面无表情的反应来放大喜剧效果。

1505
00:58:19.480 --> 00:58:24.940
But in this case, I got to pitch the comedy ball, and it felt really good.
但这次，我得以抛出喜剧的橄榄枝，感觉真的很好。

1506
00:58:25.140 --> 00:58:27.280
Other people reacted off of you.
其他人根据你的反应来演。

1507
00:58:27.480 --> 00:58:27.840
Yes.
是的。

1508
00:58:28.060 --> 00:58:29.060
And it was fun.
而且这很有趣。

1509
00:58:29.300 --> 00:58:39.480
Well, one of my favorite things to watch play out in any movie or TV show is when a character decides to step up to the plate and then bails.
嗯，我在任何电影或电视剧中最喜欢看的情节之一，就是一个角色决定迎难而上，然后却临阵脱逃了。

1510
00:58:40.960 --> 00:58:47.520
So, at the end, when Pam got out the chainsaw and was like, cutting down the competition.
所以，最后当帕姆拿出了电锯，就像是在砍掉竞争对手一样。

1511
00:58:48.040 --> 00:58:48.240
Yeah.
对。

1512
00:58:48.240 --> 00:58:49.740
The bail is my favorite.
这种临阵脱逃是我最喜欢的。

1513
00:58:49.900 --> 00:58:50.960
She's like, I'm out.
她就像是，我不干了。

1514
00:58:51.500 --> 00:58:54.320
Well, during all this, Michael has gone over to Holly's desk.
嗯，在这一切期间，迈克尔走到了霍莉的桌子旁。

1515
00:58:55.420 --> 00:58:57.980
He's stroking her yellow cardigan.
他正抚摸着她的黄色开衫。

1516
00:58:58.160 --> 00:59:00.820
He cuts half of the sleeve off.
他剪掉了半个袖子。

1517
00:59:01.040 --> 00:59:01.380
Yeah.
对。

1518
00:59:01.900 --> 00:59:03.800
That made me laugh so hard, Jenna.
这让我笑得前仰后合，珍娜。

1519
00:59:04.440 --> 00:59:13.920
And then he, like, pushes the chair in, and this screensaver pops up of Martin Short, which is so perfect.
然后他，把椅子推进去，弹出了马丁·肖特的屏幕保护程序，这太完美了。

1520
00:59:14.100 --> 00:59:15.140
As Ed Grimley.
扮演埃德·格里姆利。

1521
00:59:15.400 --> 00:59:15.760
Yes.
是的。

1522
00:59:15.760 --> 00:59:18.280
You know what Randy Cordray told me?
你知道兰迪·科德雷跟我说了什么吗？

1523
00:59:18.420 --> 00:59:18.680
What?
说什么？

1524
00:59:19.120 --> 00:59:20.240
That little moment.
那个小细节。

1525
00:59:20.700 --> 00:59:21.940
Like, that was a whole thing.
就像，那是一整套工序。

1526
00:59:22.120 --> 00:59:24.860
He said we had this graphic artist on staff.
他说我们剧组有一个平面设计师。

1527
00:59:24.860 --> 00:59:26.140
His name was Michael Marcus.
他叫迈克尔·马库斯。

1528
00:59:26.140 --> 00:59:35.240
And he had to build that on-screen computer graphic where there were these documents on the homepage, that picture of Martin Short.
他必须制作那个屏幕上的电脑图形，主页上有这些文档，还有那张马丁·肖特的照片。

1529
00:59:35.460 --> 00:59:40.020
They had to get permission to license that photo from Getty Images.
他们必须获得盖蒂图片社的授权许可才能使用那张照片。

1530
00:59:40.700 --> 00:59:45.320
I mean, that little moment, that was someone's day creating that.
我的意思是，那个小细节，那是某人花了一整天创作出来的。

1531
00:59:45.500 --> 00:59:45.550
Right.
没错。

1532
00:59:45.550 --> 00:59:48.620
And I just, I love watching the show and thinking of those details.
而我就是喜欢看这部剧，然后想到这些细节。

1533
00:59:49.300 --> 00:59:54.200
Well, to finish out the Nashua Branch storyline, Pam and Michael, they pack up.
嗯，为了结束纳什亚分公司的故事线，帕姆和迈克尔收拾行李离开。

1534
00:59:54.320 --> 00:59:55.660
I love when Pam was like, don't look up.
我喜欢帕姆说“别抬头”的时候。

1535
00:59:55.780 --> 00:59:56.360
Don't look up.
别抬头。

1536
00:59:56.480 --> 00:59:58.220
Don't look up when they're packing up the car.
当他们把行李装车时别抬头。

1537
00:59:58.780 --> 01:00:00.100
And they go to a diner.
然后他们去了一家餐馆。

1538
01:00:00.100 --> 01:00:09.500
And Michael confesses that, A, he cut off part of her sweater and that he saw a Dear Michael folder on her desktop.
迈克尔坦白说，第一，他剪了她毛衣的一部分，第二，他在她的桌面上看到一个“致迈克尔”的文件夹。

1539
01:00:09.500 --> 01:00:10.640
And he copied it.
而且他复制了它。

1540
01:00:10.820 --> 01:00:11.720
He's got it.
他拿到了。

1541
01:00:12.240 --> 01:00:14.440
And Pam says, you can't read that.
帕姆说，你不能读那个。

1542
01:00:14.960 --> 01:00:16.180
But I can read it.
但我可以读。

1543
01:00:16.860 --> 01:00:17.260
Right.
对。

1544
01:00:17.340 --> 01:00:18.060
Pam can read it.
帕姆可以读。

1545
01:00:18.120 --> 01:00:22.600
And I won't tell you what the specifics are, but I can tell you if she still likes you.
而且我不会告诉你具体内容是什么，但我可以告诉你她是否还喜欢你。

1546
01:00:22.840 --> 01:00:24.860
We had a lot of fan mail about that.
我们收到了很多关于这部分的粉丝来信。

1547
01:00:25.060 --> 01:00:27.440
Emma S., Eric M., and Zachary C.
埃玛·S、埃里克·M和扎卡里·C

1548
01:00:27.640 --> 01:00:30.180
all wanted to know, was there a letter?
都想知道，真的有信吗？

1549
01:00:30.580 --> 01:00:33.160
Or was I just pretending to read something?
还是我只是假装在读什么东西？

1550
01:00:33.840 --> 01:00:34.860
There was a letter.
确实有一封信。

1551
01:00:35.260 --> 01:00:36.640
I wondered that, too.
我也这么想过。

1552
01:00:36.840 --> 01:00:39.060
Phil Shea wrote a letter, and I was very grateful.
菲尔·谢伊写了一封信，我非常感激。

1553
01:00:40.000 --> 01:00:44.580
Because as I read it, it helped me get in a headspace.
因为当我读到它时，它帮我进入了一种状态。

1554
01:00:44.880 --> 01:00:52.420
Because there were all these things I read, but then I knew I was going to tell Michael the scripted lines of, like, it's not over.
因为我读了所有这些内容，但我知道我要对迈克尔说那些台词，比如，还没结束呢。

1555
01:00:53.320 --> 01:00:54.200
And it was great.
这太棒了。

1556
01:00:54.500 --> 01:00:58.620
It was so helpful as an actor to have not just a blank screen there.
作为演员，眼前不只是一张空白的屏幕，这太有帮助了。

1557
01:00:58.760 --> 01:01:00.680
So thank you, Phil Shea, for writing me a letter.
所以谢谢你，菲尔·谢伊，给我写了一封信。

1558
01:01:00.880 --> 01:01:05.200
I wonder if Phil had to consult the writing staff and say, guys, I'm going to write this letter.
我想知道菲尔是不是得去问问编剧团队，说，伙计们，我要写这封信了。

1559
01:01:05.360 --> 01:01:05.800
Do you have any?
你们有什么意见吗？

1560
01:01:05.940 --> 01:01:07.420
Or he just did that on his own.
还是说他只是自己这么做的。

1561
01:01:07.420 --> 01:01:09.540
I think that was stuff he just did on his own.
我觉得那是他自己做的事。

1562
01:01:09.660 --> 01:01:13.040
He was a very detail-oriented prop master.
他是一个非常注重细节的道具师。

1563
01:01:13.260 --> 01:01:13.540
Yes.
是的。

1564
01:01:13.680 --> 01:01:17.040
And he would often do that if we had a fakie piece of paper.
如果我们有一张假的纸条，他通常也会这么做。

1565
01:01:17.260 --> 01:01:17.780
A memo.
一份备忘录。

1566
01:01:18.300 --> 01:01:19.500
It was very detailed.
非常详细。

1567
01:01:19.780 --> 01:01:20.100
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1568
01:01:20.480 --> 01:01:21.760
I have a question for you.
我有个问题想问你。

1569
01:01:21.820 --> 01:01:25.500
Because when I watch this, I am always, like, relating it back to, like, things happening.
因为当我看到这里时，我总是会把它和正在发生的事情联系起来。

1570
01:01:25.980 --> 01:01:27.120
Would you have read it?
你会去读吗？

1571
01:01:27.480 --> 01:01:32.140
If you saw, like, something on your ex's computer, would you have read it?
如果你看到前任的电脑上有类似的东西，你会读吗？

1572
01:01:32.400 --> 01:01:32.800
Yeah.
会啊。

1573
01:01:33.200 --> 01:01:33.920
Me, too.
我也是。

1574
01:01:34.140 --> 01:01:34.620
Of course.
当然。

1575
01:01:35.000 --> 01:01:35.400
100%.
百分之百。

1576
01:01:35.400 --> 01:01:36.200
Yeah.
会。

1577
01:01:36.360 --> 01:01:38.320
I would have just sat down right then and there and read it.
我当时就会直接坐在那儿把它读完。

1578
01:01:38.540 --> 01:01:38.660
Correct.
没错。

1579
01:01:39.180 --> 01:01:39.460
Okay.
好吧。

1580
01:01:39.460 --> 01:01:40.640
I feel better now.
我现在感觉好多了。

1581
01:01:41.000 --> 01:01:41.180
Yeah.
是啊。

1582
01:01:41.880 --> 01:01:46.800
Well, listen, Michael is thrilled to find out that it's not over with Holly.
听着，迈克尔发现他和霍莉还没完，兴奋得不得了。

1583
01:01:48.020 --> 01:01:53.560
And we're not sure yet what he's going to do with that information, but he's happy to know it.
我们还不知道他要怎么利用这个消息，但他知道后很高兴。

1584
01:01:53.760 --> 01:01:55.040
He feels like he has closure.
他觉得自己释怀了。

1585
01:01:55.400 --> 01:01:55.620
Yeah.
对。

1586
01:01:55.860 --> 01:01:56.560
He does.
确实如此。

1587
01:01:56.560 --> 01:02:01.740
We haven't talked about the rest of this birthday storyline.
我们还没聊过这个生日故事线的其他部分呢。

1588
01:02:02.340 --> 01:02:05.140
Well, listen, they're not doing very well.
听着，他们过得可不太好。

1589
01:02:05.360 --> 01:02:09.240
Jim and Dwight are still trying to brainstorm the perfect party for Kelly.
吉姆和德怀特还在绞尽脑汁为凯利策划完美的派对。

1590
01:02:09.560 --> 01:02:09.740
Yeah.
对。

1591
01:02:10.260 --> 01:02:11.320
They're in the conference room.
他们正在会议室里。

1592
01:02:11.620 --> 01:02:24.560
Jim says, okay, so far, our ideal party consists of beer, fights to the death, cupcakes, blood pudding, blood, touch football, mating, charades, and, yes, horse hunting.
吉姆说，好吧，到目前为止，我们理想的派对包括啤酒、生死决斗、纸杯蛋糕、血肠、鲜血、触式橄榄球、交配、猜字谜，还有，对，猎马。

1593
01:02:25.220 --> 01:02:25.660
Yeah.
对。

1594
01:02:26.100 --> 01:02:26.880
And Dwight's like, you're right.
德怀特说，你说得对。

1595
01:02:27.000 --> 01:02:27.720
Forget horse hunting.
别猎马了。

1596
01:02:27.720 --> 01:02:28.300
It's stupid.
太蠢了。

1597
01:02:29.500 --> 01:02:31.220
Just only lose that one.
只要去掉这一个就行。

1598
01:02:31.380 --> 01:02:31.480
Yeah.
对。

1599
01:02:31.480 --> 01:02:32.740
All the rest are viable.
其余的全都切实可行。

1600
01:02:33.060 --> 01:02:33.240
Yeah.
对。

1601
01:02:33.340 --> 01:02:34.640
All the rest sound great.
其余的听起来都很棒。

1602
01:02:34.900 --> 01:02:38.540
But ultimately, they actually find a theme.
但归根结底，他们确实找到一个主题。

1603
01:02:39.380 --> 01:02:39.700
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1604
01:02:40.160 --> 01:02:41.940
Everyone gathers in the conference room.
大家聚集在会议室里。

1605
01:02:42.140 --> 01:02:43.000
Kelly comes in.
凯莉进来了。

1606
01:02:43.240 --> 01:02:44.040
There's a cake.
有个蛋糕。

1607
01:02:44.200 --> 01:02:45.320
Her name is spelled wrong.
她的名字拼错了。

1608
01:02:45.480 --> 01:02:45.800
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1609
01:02:45.940 --> 01:02:46.880
And there's a chiclet.
还有一块口香糖。

1610
01:02:47.460 --> 01:02:48.760
You know what a chiclet is?
你知道什么是口香糖豆吗？

1611
01:02:48.900 --> 01:02:49.380
I do.
我知道。

1612
01:02:49.500 --> 01:02:51.140
It's a piece of gum and it's a square.
它是一块口香糖，而且是方的。

1613
01:02:51.140 --> 01:02:52.780
It's a little square piece of gum.
是一小块方形的口香糖。

1614
01:02:53.040 --> 01:02:54.160
I love a chiclet.
我很喜欢这种口香糖。

1615
01:02:54.180 --> 01:02:55.060
I love a chiclet, too.
我也很喜欢。

1616
01:02:55.060 --> 01:02:58.080
I like it that it has like a candy coating before I chew the gum.
我喜欢嚼口香糖前外面那层糖衣的感觉。

1617
01:02:58.180 --> 01:02:59.080
I like the crunch.
我喜欢那种脆脆的口感。

1618
01:02:59.360 --> 01:02:59.740
Me, too.
我也是。

1619
01:03:00.420 --> 01:03:02.560
Kelly wants to know what's up with the chiclet.
凯莉想知道这口香糖是怎么回事。

1620
01:03:02.840 --> 01:03:04.960
Jim says, that's the best part.
吉姆说，这才是最棒的部分。

1621
01:03:05.280 --> 01:03:07.380
The chiclet represents a pillow.
口香糖代表一个枕头。

1622
01:03:07.640 --> 01:03:09.540
It's a pillow or a television.
是一个枕头或一台电视。

1623
01:03:10.060 --> 01:03:10.980
That's our theme.
这就是我们的主题。

1624
01:03:11.320 --> 01:03:14.020
A pillow or a television is their theme.
枕头或电视就是他们的主题。

1625
01:03:14.260 --> 01:03:17.380
She gets to decide one hour of TV or an hour of napping.
她可以决定看一小时电视或睡一小时午觉。

1626
01:03:17.380 --> 01:03:18.620
What would you pick?
你会选哪个？

1627
01:03:18.980 --> 01:03:22.080
I would, oh, I don't know if I could sleep at work.
我会，哦，我不知道我能不能在公司睡觉。

1628
01:03:22.320 --> 01:03:24.460
I can't nap in general.
我一般无法午睡。

1629
01:03:24.460 --> 01:03:27.540
I have to be sick in order to take a nap.
我必须生病了才能睡个午觉。

1630
01:03:27.700 --> 01:03:32.660
Even if I've gotten three hours of sleep the night before, I can't nap.
即使我前一晚只睡了三个小时，我也无法午睡。

1631
01:03:32.900 --> 01:03:33.180
Same.
我也是。

1632
01:03:33.180 --> 01:03:34.980
I get like wired tired.
我会变成那种极度疲惫却又很亢奋的状态。

1633
01:03:35.360 --> 01:03:40.160
So, I mean, I'm in the middle of the White Lotus.
所以，我的意思是，我正在看《白莲花度假村》。

1634
01:03:40.240 --> 01:03:42.080
I'm in the middle of Hacks.
我正在看《绝望hacks》。

1635
01:03:42.420 --> 01:03:45.080
I only just finished Mare of Easttown.
我才刚看完《东城梦魇》。

1636
01:03:45.220 --> 01:03:46.720
Do you hear how behind I am?
你听得出我落后多少进度了吧？

1637
01:03:47.420 --> 01:03:50.580
So, hour of TV, yes, please.
所以，看一小时电视，好啊，求之不得。

1638
01:03:50.840 --> 01:03:52.040
That sounds decadent to me.
这对我来说听起来太奢侈了。

1639
01:03:52.500 --> 01:03:54.740
Also, yeah, I can't sleep during the day.
而且，对啊，我白天睡不着觉。

1640
01:03:54.900 --> 01:03:57.440
Something has to be wrong with me if I fall asleep during the day.
如果我大白天睡着了，那一定是我身体出问题了。

1641
01:03:57.560 --> 01:03:57.720
Yeah.
是啊。

1642
01:03:57.720 --> 01:03:59.200
It's just like my body just won't do it.
就好像我的身体根本不允许我这么做。

1643
01:03:59.700 --> 01:04:03.300
I do think this is a little bit of an old tech alert.
我觉得这有点像是老旧科技警报。

1644
01:04:03.580 --> 01:04:04.660
What's the old tech?
什么是老旧科技？

1645
01:04:04.960 --> 01:04:09.560
They say that the chiclet represents a pillow or a television.
他们说口香糖代表枕头或电视。

1646
01:04:10.080 --> 01:04:10.460
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1647
01:04:10.820 --> 01:04:15.260
And I think at work now, we would just watch an hour on our phone or our computer.
我觉得现在在公司，我们大概只会用手机或电脑看一小时。

1648
01:04:15.480 --> 01:04:16.100
That's true.
确实如此。

1649
01:04:16.100 --> 01:04:19.740
And also, doesn't Stanley say there's nothing good on right now?
而且，斯坦利不是说过现在没什么好看的节目吗？

1650
01:04:20.080 --> 01:04:22.720
Well, Creed says Bonnie Hunt's on.
哦，克里德说邦妮·亨特正在播。

1651
01:04:22.900 --> 01:04:25.780
But it's that they're going to watch like live television.
但它们会像看直播电视一样去观看。

1652
01:04:25.920 --> 01:04:26.440
That's right.
没错。

1653
01:04:26.600 --> 01:04:27.880
Not streaming anything.
什么都不流媒体播放。

1654
01:04:27.880 --> 01:04:28.760
No streaming.
不流媒体播放。

1655
01:04:29.060 --> 01:04:29.380
Mm-mm.
嗯嗯。

1656
01:04:29.700 --> 01:04:33.200
So, I would say their theme was a little bit of an old tech alert.
所以，我觉得他们的主题有点像老科技警报。

1657
01:04:33.440 --> 01:04:33.940
I agree.
我同意。

1658
01:04:34.380 --> 01:04:36.300
Well, Kelly chooses nap.
好吧，凯莉选择了小睡。

1659
01:04:36.420 --> 01:04:39.240
And she takes a little nap under the conference table.
她在会议桌下小睡了一会儿。

1660
01:04:39.460 --> 01:04:45.220
And while she does, Jim and Dwight sit on that little couch by reception.
在她这么做的时候，吉姆和德怀特坐在接待处旁边的那张小沙发上。

1661
01:04:45.220 --> 01:04:46.460
And they eat their cake.
他们吃着蛋糕。

1662
01:04:46.460 --> 01:04:47.980
And they're very proud of themselves.
他们对自己感到非常骄傲。

1663
01:04:48.280 --> 01:04:50.800
And I want to point out this scene to everyone.
我想向大家指出这个场景。

1664
01:04:51.320 --> 01:04:58.880
Because John is doing a classic fakey, eaty acting technique with this cake.
因为约翰在这个蛋糕场景中使用了经典的假吃表演技巧。

1665
01:04:59.120 --> 01:05:00.840
He's shoving the food around the plate.
他在盘子里推挤着食物。

1666
01:05:00.840 --> 01:05:03.960
He would take a big scoop of cake.
他会舀起很大一勺蛋糕。

1667
01:05:04.240 --> 01:05:07.640
But then, he smushes it back down.
但随后，他又把它压回盘子里。

1668
01:05:07.880 --> 01:05:12.200
And so, by the time he puts it in his mouth, it just has a little frosting on it.
所以，等他把它放进嘴里时，上面其实只有一点糖霜。

1669
01:05:12.320 --> 01:05:12.600
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1670
01:05:12.820 --> 01:05:13.460
Watch it.
看这个。

1671
01:05:13.620 --> 01:05:17.900
He goes for the cake three times and never actually eats a piece.
他去拿了三次蛋糕，却从来没有真正吃上一块。

1672
01:05:18.200 --> 01:05:20.540
At the beginning, he eats like half a piece.
一开始，他吃了一半左右。

1673
01:05:21.140 --> 01:05:24.560
You have to do this because otherwise you're going to get sick.
你必须这样做，否则你会生病的。

1674
01:05:25.280 --> 01:05:30.060
However, sitting next to him is Rainn Wilson, who eats the cake.
然而，坐在他旁边的是雷恩·威尔逊，他可是真吃蛋糕。

1675
01:05:30.420 --> 01:05:30.940
Rainn?
雷恩？

1676
01:05:30.940 --> 01:05:32.700
Because Rainn always ate in scenes.
因为雷恩在拍戏时总是吃东西。

1677
01:05:32.900 --> 01:05:33.560
It didn't matter.
这无所谓。

1678
01:05:33.820 --> 01:05:35.940
Remember, he ate so many bananas, he got sick.
记得吗，他吃了那么多香蕉，结果吃病了。

1679
01:05:36.140 --> 01:05:36.340
Yeah.
是啊。

1680
01:05:36.780 --> 01:05:39.580
When Rainn, as Dwight, does anything, he goes all out.
当雷恩饰演德怀特时，他做什么都是全力以赴。

1681
01:05:39.760 --> 01:05:39.920
Yep.
没错。

1682
01:05:40.220 --> 01:05:44.580
And I feel like Rainn eats in scenes the way Brad Pitt eats in movies.
我觉得雷恩在剧中的吃相，就像布拉德·皮特在电影里的吃相一样。

1683
01:05:44.980 --> 01:05:46.460
Watch in Ocean's 12.
看《十一罗汉》续集。

1684
01:05:46.720 --> 01:05:47.940
The guy is always eating.
这家伙总是在吃东西。

1685
01:05:48.160 --> 01:05:49.880
I wanted to know, like, is this a choice?
我想知道，这算是一种选择吗？

1686
01:05:49.880 --> 01:05:51.580
You're constantly eating something.
你一直在吃东西。

1687
01:05:51.780 --> 01:05:52.880
Watch Goodfellas.
看《好家伙》。

1688
01:05:53.000 --> 01:05:55.460
Do you see how much steak and pasta those guys eat?
你看到那些家伙吃了多少牛排和意面吗？

1689
01:05:55.620 --> 01:05:56.680
They dig in.
他们大快朵颐。

1690
01:05:56.900 --> 01:05:58.100
Goodfellas makes me hungry.
《好家伙》看得我直饿。

1691
01:05:58.340 --> 01:05:58.700
Yeah.
对啊。

1692
01:05:58.820 --> 01:06:00.060
When I watch it, I get hungry.
我看的时候就会饿。

1693
01:06:00.220 --> 01:06:00.640
For sure.
确实。

1694
01:06:01.440 --> 01:06:03.200
Guys, guess what?
伙计们，猜猜怎么着？

1695
01:06:03.460 --> 01:06:05.460
That was Lecture Circuit Part 2.
那是《讲座巡回演出》第二部分。

1696
01:06:05.800 --> 01:06:06.200
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1697
01:06:06.520 --> 01:06:08.500
With a little bit of movie.
带有一点电影色彩。

1698
01:06:08.620 --> 01:06:09.240
Extra stuff.
额外的内容。

1699
01:06:09.360 --> 01:06:10.140
Extra stuff.
额外的内容。

1700
01:06:10.300 --> 01:06:14.720
We had, I felt like, a lot of interesting movie magic facts.
我觉得我们有很多有趣的电影魔术冷知识。

1701
01:06:15.060 --> 01:06:18.760
A lot of cat grooming facts.
许多关于猫咪美容的冷知识。

1702
01:06:19.180 --> 01:06:20.820
And a Forrest Gump impression.
还有一个阿甘正传的模仿秀。

1703
01:06:21.260 --> 01:06:21.580
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1704
01:06:21.960 --> 01:06:22.940
Not a bad day.
这日子过得真不错。

1705
01:06:23.220 --> 01:06:24.320
Not too shabby.
还算凑合。

1706
01:06:24.480 --> 01:06:27.000
And next week is Blood Drive.
下周是献血车活动。

1707
01:06:27.300 --> 01:06:27.660
Oh, yeah.
哦，对。

1708
01:06:28.380 --> 01:06:30.640
I've got some good facts about the Blood Mobile.
我有一些关于献血车的有趣事实。

1709
01:06:31.060 --> 01:06:32.540
It was actually on the set.
其实就在片场。

1710
01:06:32.720 --> 01:06:33.120
It was.
是的。

1711
01:06:33.140 --> 01:06:33.880
It was in the parking lot.
就在停车场。

1712
01:06:33.980 --> 01:06:34.580
A real one.
一辆真正的献血车。

1713
01:06:34.700 --> 01:06:34.880
Yep.
没错。

1714
01:06:35.180 --> 01:06:35.340
Yep.
没错。

1715
01:06:35.480 --> 01:06:36.800
I'll tell you all about it next week.
下周我会在节目里详细讲讲。

1716
